From 27935b3128126b48d28da5a10226eb2804cfcc44 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim Besard <tim.besard@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 10:00:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add clSetCPUMaxComputeUnitsPOCL to size the CPU devices
 without the environment

Applications that embed PoCL may want to choose how many worker threads
the CPU devices start, e.g., to match their own thread pool. The only way
to do that was to set POCL_CPU_MAX_CU_COUNT, but changing the environment
of a running process isn't thread-safe, is inherited by child processes,
and affects every copy of PoCL loaded in the process.

The new cl_pocl_cpu_compute_units platform extension adds
clSetCPUMaxComputeUnitsPOCL(platform, num_compute_units). It takes
precedence over the environment variables, and must be called before the
devices are initialized; afterwards it returns CL_INVALID_OPERATION.
